// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-030
=adr: 030
=title: Derived State as Sub-Document via Regular Collection with TTL
=date: 2026-02-25
=status: superseded_by=ADR-031

#ctx
~blocker: device_states time series collection blocks ADR-028 (no post-insert $set)
~ADR-029_workaround: separate device_derived_states collection → second DB read + collection maintenance + conceptual fragmentation

#decision
=chosen: convert device_states from time series → regular MongoDB collection with TTL index
=remove_timeseries: timeseries:{timeField,metaField,granularity} config removed
=add_ttl: expireAfterSeconds=157680000 on {timestamp:1} (5yr EPA)
=add_derived_field: derived:Schema.Types.Mixed default:{}
=upsertDerived: DeviceState.updateOne({_id:stateId},{$set:{'derived.<key>':value}})
=getLatest: single query (derived already on doc)
=deleted: [device_derived_states collection, DeviceDerivedState model]
!unchanged: [display_rule derived??data, React_Query_strategy, WS_broadcast_format, RealTimeGaugeBlock_Number()_coerce, $dateTrunc_aggregations]

#superseded_reason: ADR-031 reverts device_states back to time series for data governance reasons; device_derived_states restored

#scope
=arch_summary_update: no
